# Sitemaps are generated into public/ by `sitemap:generate` every six hours.
# They are build output, not source: the catalogue files run to ~8 MB each, and
# a stale copy committed here would be deployed over the fresh one and served
# ahead of the routes — FrankenPHP answers with any real file in public/ before
# PHP is reached.
/public/sitemap*.xml

# The rule above only ever applied to files git was not already tracking, and
# public/sitemap.xml had been committed before it was written — so every
# `sitemap:generate` on the server left the working tree dirty and the next
# `git pull` refused to run. Untracked here on 28.08.2026; the root .gitignore
# already carried a one-off line for sitemap-news.xml, which is the same
# papercut patched once for the one file that hurt first.

# What Octane installs and runs with, and what plugins publish into public/.
#
# All of it is generated on the machine it runs on: `octane:install
# --server=frankenphp` writes the worker, downloads the 149 MB binary beside
# artisan, and FrankenPHP keeps its Caddy state in caddy/. `filament:assets`
# and the jobs-monitor plugin publish theirs under public/.
#
# None of it belongs in the repository, and leaving it untracked is not free:
# `git status` on the server listed five real files as junk alongside five
# genuine accidents — captured tinker output with names like `);exit` — and
# the binary holding port 8000 was one keystroke from being cleaned up with
# them. Untracked files also blocked a `git pull` here once already, which is
# the same papercut the sitemap rule above was written for.
/frankenphp
/caddy/
/public/frankenphp-worker.php
/public/js/app/
/public/css/croustibat/
